//
// Conventions
// - Int identity primary keys; public-facing identifiers (registration numbers, payment
//   references, exam attempt ids) are separate random/sequential codes.
// - SQL Server has no enums: status/type columns are NVARCHAR and the allowed values
//   live in src/lib/constants.ts and are validated with zod before every write.
// - SQL Server rejects multiple cascade paths, so relations default to NoAction and
//   only leaf/child tables cascade. Records with history are archived, never deleted.
